       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1000 mg of sertraline once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or CNS effects. It may be a typo for 100 mg.\n\nTypical adult dosing:\n- **Starting dose:** 25\u201350 mg by mouth once daily. For depression, OCD, or PTSD, 50 mg is common. For panic disorder or social anxiety, start at 25 mg.\n- **Usual range:** 50\u2013200 mg once daily.\n- **Maximum:** 200 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose you intended, for example 50 mg or 100 mg PO daily, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1000 mg, for example because of an overdose or a different drug, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist before ordering."
