      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the clinical picture. 1000 mg/day is five times the maximum dose, and I have no indication that would justify it. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere's how to move forward:\n- **Talk to your resident or attending.** Dosing like this should be reviewed by a licensed prescriber. If they intend it, they can enter it themselves or tell you exactly what they want.\n- **Call pharmacy.** They can check the intended dose and help with a safe regimen.\n- **If the patient may have taken an overdose,** that's a toxicology and poison control issue, not a standing order. Contact poison control at 1-800-222-1222 in the US, or your local toxicology service.\n\nIf the intended dose was within the normal range, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily, tell me and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
